    readme.md
        1→Superstruct makes it easy to define interfaces and then validate JavaScript data against them. Its type annotation API was inspired by [TypeScript](https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/basic-types.html), [Flow](https://flow.org/en/docs/types/), [Go](https://gobyexample.com/structs), and [GraphQL](http://graphql.org/learn/schema/), giving it a familiar and easy to understand API.
        7→### Usage
        9→Superstruct allows you to define the shape of data you want to validate:
